      "writtenOn": "2023-06-30T18:28:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fallback logic is not obvious to me. I believe you that OpenSSH tries public key auth first and certificate auth second, but what if that changes? Won\u0027t we end up testing certificate auth twice?\n\nCan\u0027t we write \"rsa.pub\", test, delete it, write \"rsa-cert.pub\", test?",
      "revId": "e83ad4d2f146adbfd993c8904f22840891c1ed99",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa7d05ff_7f152b74",
        "filename": "ssh/test/sshcli_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 35201
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-01T14:10:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now we only store rsa-cert.pub before certificate authentication.\nWe can\u0027t remove rsa.pub because in this case OpenSSH prints these logs\n\ndebug3: sign_and_send_pubkey: RSA-CERT SHA256:Anr3LjZK8YVpjrxu79myrW9Hrb/wpcMNpVvTq/RcBm8\ndebug1: sign_and_send_pubkey: no separate private key for certificate \"rsa\"\n\ninstead of these ones\n\ndebug3: sign_and_send_pubkey: RSA-CERT SHA256:Anr3LjZK8YVpjrxu79myrW9Hrb/wpcMNpVvTq/RcBm8\ndebug2: sign_and_send_pubkey: using private key \"rsa\" for certificate\n\nthe logic is unchanged but without rsa.pub the signature algorithm and format are as expected, so the test will also work with OpenSSH 7.2-7.7.\n\nThe test server stores the number of successful public key and certificate authentications and they are checked in the test case.\nIf the public key or certificate authentication fails, the test will fail.",
      "parentUuid": "e48e8984_0a74f7f9",
      "revId": "e83ad4d2f146adbfd993c8904f22840891c1ed99",
